### Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension (click "Send Request").
### Otherwise copy into Postman.

### 1. Inventory: list products (Laptop=1 at 60000, Mouse=2 at 500)
GET http://localhost:8082/products

### 2. Inventory: add a product
POST http://localhost:8082/products
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Keyboard", "price": 1500, "stock": 25 }

### 3. Inventory: set stock for product 2
PUT http://localhost:8082/inventory/2?quantity=50

### 4. Order service: list users (user 1 is seeded)
GET http://localhost:8081/users

### 5. Order service: create a user
POST http://localhost:8081/users
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Asha" }

### 6. Place an order that SUCCEEDS (2 mice = 1000)
POST http://localhost:8081/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": 1, "productId": 2, "quantity": 2 }

### 7. Place an order that FAILS payment (1 laptop = 60000, rule: fail above 50000)
POST http://localhost:8081/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": 1, "productId": 1, "quantity": 1 }

### 8. Place an order with too much quantity (expect 409 from inventory)
POST http://localhost:8081/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": 1, "productId": 2, "quantity": 9999 }

### 9. Check orders (status moves PENDING_PAYMENT -> PAID or PAYMENT_FAILED)
GET http://localhost:8081/orders

### 10. Check payments
GET http://localhost:8083/payments

### 11. Check stock again (laptop stock returns after the failed payment)
GET http://localhost:8082/products
